{
  "_doc": "Candidate Priority Intelligence Requirements (PIRs), refined framework CD-2a, held in config for SHADOW tagging only (flag PIR_TAGGING_SHADOW_V1, default off). Priority A = national/systemic resilience; Priority B = professional/sector (regulated industries); X = cross-cutting product trust. No PIR depends on any organisation's own technology estate: relevance is judged on national, systemic and sector grounds, and international developments qualify on leading-indicator or transferable-lesson grounds without demonstrated Australian impact. Matching is lexical and deterministic (word-boundary, case-insensitive) over item title/summary plus structured classifier fields; it never changes selection, ranking or delivery. Fields: terms = any one is sufficient; event_types = sufficient on their own; context = list of [group_a, group_b] where one term from EACH group is needed. Match strength: a term or context hit is STRONG; an event_type-only match is WEAK (a stored type can be wrong), and an item whose only matches are weak and that is high severity stays in the unmatched high-severity lane.",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "approved_shadow_tagging_baseline",
